// board.mn — the medium's standing verdict on its own source.
//
// A BOARD LINE is a named invariant of the wheel, the bound it may not cross,
// and the SITES the medium finds for it live. Every line's sites come from
// `census_sites` — the same walk `mentl <file> census <shape>`
// projects — so the board asks the medium a question the medium already
// answers, and nothing between the two re-derives it. The count is `len` of
// that list and is never stored beside it.
//
// WHAT THIS REPLACES, and why the replacement is the point rather than the
// tidying. The bounds lived in `tools/verify-baseline.txt`: 1,695 lines
// holding 26 numbers, 1,669 of them prose justifying those numbers. Each
// check ran the medium, RENDERED the count to a sentence, re-parsed the
// sentence with a regex, and compared the result against a number grepped
// out of that file. Three re-derivations of one fact — the count the walk
// had already computed, the bound the project had already decided, and the
// verdict a shell `if` then invented. The prose was the deepest loss: a
// bound's justification is a Reason, and a Reason belongs on the node it
// justifies, so each bound below carries its own — walkable by `mentl why`,
// rendered as its `Lede:` at its own address, and impossible to separate
// from the number it explains.
//
// WHAT A BOUND IS NOT. A bound is not a proof. Fourteen of the old file's
// keys read ZERO, and a ratchet held at zero is a proxy for a proof nobody
// minted (PLAN §7, in those words). The ultimate form of every line here is
// its own DELETION: the shape becomes a `DiagKind` the executable refuses,
// `diag_refuses` holds the invariant directly, and the line retires the way
// the use-after-move ratchet did at pin 21696779. So this roster is a COUNTDOWN,
// and a line that never falls is not a passing gate — it is 8.4's universal
// executable refusal, unbuilt, saying so.
import types

import query

// One measured invariant: the shape the medium counts and the count it may
// not exceed. The two fields are inseparable — a shape with no bound is a
// report, and a bound with no shape is the text file this replaces.
type Bound = {ceiling: Int, shape: CensusShape}

// What the medium found when it looked: the SITES, not a count of them.
//
// This arm carried an `Int` for one day and the Int was a COPY — `census_sites`
// returns the located list and the count is `len` of it, so storing the number
// beside the list it came from is the Carried-Truth violation this module was
// written to end, committed inside the module that ends it. The list rides both
// arms because a board that only speaks when it fails cannot show a countdown
// moving, and the falling number is the whole reason these lines exist.
//
// It is also what lets a breach say WHICH — a bound that reports "367, was 365"
// tells the developer a number rose; a bound that names its sites tells them
// where to look, from a list the walk already built and the verb used to throw
// away.
type Standing = Within([Int]) | Over([Int])

// The roster, complete by construction: a shape absent here is not measured,
// which is visible, where a shape measured against a missing bound would be
// a silent pass. Each entry's prose is its justification — the `why` the old
// file kept 1,669 lines away from the number it belonged to.
fn board_bounds() with Memory + Alloc = [
  // Zero because an eta-wrapper is a REFERENCE written as a MINT: the name it
  // wraps already exists, so the lambda re-mints what a handle would have
  // carried. Retires when the shape is a refusal rather than a count.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, shape: CsEta}),
  // The one line here that is genuinely a COUNTDOWN rather than a held zero.
  //
  // ITS CONVICTION IS RE-FOUNDED, and the text it replaces was mine from one
  // pin ago: "every effectful lambda is a row denied its decl home." That is
  // REFUTED at the artifact — `mentl <file>:<line>` at a lambda renders its
  // row, so the row has a home; what it lacks is a NAME, and the address
  // surface reaches it either way. The honest conviction is narrower and can
  // actually reach zero: a REFERENCE WRITTEN AS A MINT. Measured over this
  // very census, half these sites are `(x) => match x { … }` — pattern
  // dispatch paying a wrapper to reach the arm list the language already has
  // (`Hβ.syntax.function-literal-is-an-arm-list`) — and 102 more are a call
  // whose params pass straight through, which is a hole. Neither is anonymity;
  // both are a mint where an edge belonged.
  //
  // IT HAS MOVED IN BOTH DIRECTIONS AND BOTH MOVES ARE RECORDED HERE, beside
  // the number, rather than argued in a file the number could drift from.
  // 365 -> 367 when this verb landed: `infer_context` takes a THUNK, so every
  // route that judges pays one lambda, and each `VerbSpec` carries the
  // argument parser its table is built from — structural, one per sibling,
  // not authored anonymity. Then 367 -> 236, which is the arm-list literal's
  // payoff read rather than assumed: the sweep converted the pattern-dispatch
  // half of the corpus and the census stopped convicting a form that carries
  // no param list at all, so 131 sites left the conviction honestly.
  //
  // The ceiling follows the measurement DOWN. A ratchet that only ever rises
  // to meet a breach has stopped ratcheting, and this one sat 131 above its
  // own subject for a full landing before anyone read the WITHIN line — which
  // is the argument for a board that reports the counts it is inside, not
  // only the ones it is over.
  Bound({ceiling: 236, shape: CsEffectfulLambda}),
  // A record pattern whose receiver row never closes reads a field offset
  // the graph cannot prove. `T_FieldOffsetUnprovable` reports that class at
  // the receiver now; this line retires when that diagnostic arms.
  //
  // SEEN RED AT 14 on 2026-09-21, and it was right: fourteen `{path, ...}`
  // puns over the module cell, all inside lambdas under `any`/`find`, and
  // the binary built from them trapped in `cost` and printed nothing in
  // `doc` — the neighbouring-field read, measured. The zero here is what
  // caught it; the readers went through closed projections (`cell_path`)
  // and the count came back to zero. The pun returns when the row union
  // lands (`Hβ.infer.record-row-vars-are-not-unioned`).
  Bound({ceiling: 0, shape: CsRecordPatternOpen}),
  // Drift mode 10 — the nine survivors are documented sentinels, not masked
  // cases. Every wildcard that is NOT one of them is a variant the author
  // declined to enumerate, and the medium cannot tell the difference, which
  // is exactly why the bound is a count and not zero.
  Bound({ceiling: 9, shape: CsWildcardZero}),
  // Drift mode 13 — a bug is zero or it is blocking; a masked failure is the
  // surrender-fallback Anchor 2 deletes rather than wraps.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, shape: CsFailureMask}),
  // A print inside a `report(...)` arm corrupts WAT stdout — the wheel's own
  // emission running through the same file descriptor as its narration.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, shape: CsPrintInReport}),
  // Drift mode 10's typed face: a wildcard arm minting `Forall`, a bare
  // `TVar`, `"Pure"` or `""` is a fabricated judgment, and a fabricated
  // judgment is indistinguishable downstream from a proven one.
  //
  // 21 → 65 on 2026-09-21, and the rise is the roster WIDENING, not the
  // wheel worsening: `_ => []` joined it — "this kind carries nothing", the
  // fabricated absence over a load-bearing ADT, found where it had hidden
  // that a `let`, a refinement and an alias declare names (so an import
  // used only for one of them read as dead). Forty-four such arms stood the
  // day the roster grew; each retires by enumeration.
  Bound({ceiling: 65, shape: CsWildcardFabricates}),
  // Drift mode 15 — a value given a leading-underscore name instead of being
  // deleted. The rename silences the reader, never the fact that nothing
  // reads it.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, shape: CsUnderscoreRetain}),
  // Drift mode 8 — an int-coded flag is an ADT the author did not write, and
  // every comparison against it is a claim the type system cannot check.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, shape: CsFlagAsInt}),
  // Drift mode 7 — adjacent `x, x_h` parameters are one record split across
  // two positions, with position standing in for the identity the record
  // would have carried.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, shape: CsParallelArrays}),
  // Drift mode 1 — a dispatch-slot record. The word never appears in correct
  // Mentl: the graph plus a handler IS the form a vtable approximates.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, shape: CsVtableRecord}),
  // Drift mode 2 — scope as a parent-pointer frame stack. Env lookup is an
  // effect op; a frame walk is that op re-implemented where the handler was.
  Bound({ceiling: 0, shape: CsEnvFrame}),
  // THE SECOND LINE ON THIS ROSTER THAT IS A REAL COUNTDOWN, and it was an
  // OPINION until it was a number.
  //
  // A signature past `wide_row_width` names more effects than a reader can
  // hold — nineteen, at the worst site on this wheel. The conviction is not
  // that long rows are ugly. It is that each one is a capability nobody
  // named: SYNTAX's §«Named effect rows» already provides the form, so a
  // 17-name row becoming `with Judging + !Network` retires a site while
  // losing no proven fact. Under it sits the deeper claim — that the
  // POSITIVE row should be inferred and projected, and only negations, pins
  // and genuine narrowings authored — at which point the count reaches zero
  // and this line deletes itself like every other one here is supposed to.
  //
  // It was seen RED at 18 against its measured 19 before it was trusted,
  // which is the only reason it is on the board: a bound nobody has watched
  // fail is a decoration (§9.11). Then it MOVED in the same landing, 19 → 12,
  // and the move is the argument rather than the number. Seven of the
  // nineteen were the same sixteen-name core spelled seven times — the
  // whole-program judgment's capability, which had no name. `type Judging =
  // …` (src/driver.mn) gave it one, and the seven signatures became
  // `with Judging`, `+ Filesystem`, `+ Persist`, `+ Fail` — every remaining
  // name a decision a reader should read. No proven fact was lost; a row
  // alias is transparent, so the checked row is identical.
  //
  // The remaining twelve are emit, cursor, infer and synth_proposer, whose
  // cores differ from this one and from each other — each is its own unnamed
  // capability, and naming them is what walks this to zero.
  Bound({ceiling: 12, shape: CsWideRow}),
  // THE ONE BOUND ON THIS BOARD MINTED FROM A PRICE RATHER THAN A PRINCIPLE,
  // and the price was measured before the bound existed. The wheel compiles
  // itself through two links — the blob (every file concatenated, one module,
  // one whole-program judgment) and the manifest (the import DAG, which is
  // what every user's program takes) — and the manifest emits 7,969 MORE
  // lines for the same tree. Four censuses through an instrumented lower
  // reduced that to one fact: 727 extra `multishot yield floor` guards ← 702
  // extra `can_yield` ROW verdicts ← 1,580 extra `EtOpen` tail chases ← 703
  // extra edges chasing to `NRowFree`.
  //
  // NEITHER LINK IS WRONG, which is why this is a ratchet and not a refusal
  // class: a manifest-built wheel emits output byte-identical to a blob-built
  // one, so the two compilers are extensionally equal and every one of those
  // floors is provably unreachable. The blob link simply PROVES MORE. This
  // counts what the weave declines to ground, and the cost is ~8,000 dead
  // emitted lines on the link a user actually takes.
  //
  // 1,048 — AND THE NUMBER MOVED TWICE BEFORE THIS LINE SETTLED, which is
  // the part worth reading. Born at 1,041 keyed on CALL SITES, it breached on
  // its own next landing at 1,045 because four helper fns were added with not
  // one row changing. That looked like a count measuring code volume rather
  // than a defect, so it was re-keyed onto the DECLARATION and read 135.
  //
  // The re-key was WRONG and the facet built the same hour proved it: a
  // decl's own graph node, the env's generalized scheme, and the callee
  // handle at a call site are THREE rows and they disagree — `mentl <file>
  // row chase_deep` answers `tail closed` through the scheme while the
  // decl-keyed census convicted it. `can_yield` asks the third, per call
  // site, and emits a floor per call site. So the call-site count is not an
  // inflated proxy for the defect; it IS the defect's extent, and its rising
  // when code adds calls to an ungrounded callee is TRUE.
  //
  // Stability was traded for correspondence, deliberately. A ceiling that
  // rises with honest growth is worse than one that falls — and the honest
  // countdown wants the free VARIABLE as its key: every sampled site in
  // `backends/wasm` lands on ONE cell (109302), so this is far fewer causes
  // than sites. THAT SHAPE EXISTS NOW (`CsFreeRowVar`, a census read) AND IT
  // IS NOT A BOUND, for a reason the measurement supplied: on the manifest
  // link it convicts 101 cells, and 89 of them are a signature's own
  // quantified row or its per-use instantiation — the only spelling row
  // polymorphism has, so a ratchet on it would convict the language. The
  // countdown that can reach zero is the cells NO scheme quantifies, and
  // that shape reads the quantifier (`sig_owns` is where the wheel draws the
  // line). Until it is built this line prices the extent, and the extent is
  // the true cost: one floor per call.
  //
  // 1,047 — one site fell when the decls facet stopped projecting each
  // handle to a (module, span) pair at collection time: that `map` was a
  // convicted call, and it is deleted with the projection it made (a site
  // is a handle now, projected at the render). The ceiling follows the
  // count down; it never leads it.
  //
  // 1,051 — RAISED, and the reason is the whole argument for ending the
  // flat judgment. Eleven index-threaded self-calls in query.mn and graph.mn
  // became `fold`/`any`/`find`/`filter` stages (Morgan's standing rule: what
  // can be a verb chain is one), and every one of those stages is a call to
  // a row-polymorphic HOF whose row THIS link leaves free — so the iteration
  // count fell and this count rose, for the same edits. Two ratchets pulling
  // against each other is the measurement that the weave under-grounds rows
  // the flat link grounds; the cause is one judgment's order-dependence,
  // and the fix is there, never in writing fewer folds.
  // `Hβ.link.manifest-and-blob-emit-differently` is where this number falls.
  //
  // 1,060 — RAISED 2026-09-23, and the medium named every one of the nine.
  // The declaration-edge landing added calls to the address renderers
  // (`node_address`, `show_declared_at`, the doc and provider renders), and
  // each callee is a CLOSED LEAF whose row cell carries a tail another
  // judgment wrote: `mentl src/main.mn row int_to_str` answers `Alloc +
  // Memory`, tail open through cells 139064 and 139877 to the free cell
  // 151261, and `show_span` and `node_address` answer the same chain. A
  // leaf's row learning a free tail from its callers is the wrong-direction
  // write the rows landing ends (`Hβ.effects.rows-are-propagated-cells`), so
  // new calls to it are counted as convictions of that defect, not new
  // defects. A first cut had also made `site_address` part of `show_reason`'s
  // recursion (the declaration render reached its cell branch) and read
  // 1,067; the render reads the node's own address now and the cycle is gone.
  //
  // 1,075 — RAISED 2026-09-23 by fifteen, named by the medium the same way.
  // The nested coverage judgment (src/coverage.mn) is two recursive walks —
  // a pattern node to the values it takes (`space_of`) and an untaken value
  // back to the pattern that names it (`render_space` and its siblings) —
  // and twenty of their self- and sibling-calls are convicted on this link,
  // net fifteen after the four hand-walks they replaced went. No row among
  // them is authored; each is inferred and closed on the flat link, which is
  // this line's own standing defect, not a new one. Declaring their positive
  // rows by hand would ground them and is refused on purpose: SYNTAX's
  // endpoint is the positive row inferred and projected, never typed.
  //
  // 1,080 — five more, named: named constructor fields render a variant's
  // fields (format `render_variant`), lower an unread field at its cell's
  // judged type (`lower_field_cell`, two calls), and parse a field or read a
  // type application as positional fields (parser, two). Same defect, same
  // counting rule; no row among them is authored.
  //
  // 1,081 — one more, named: coverage's record witness renders its fields
  // through `render_field_spaces` (coverage:366) where it had spelled a `|>`
  // chain inside the splice — the shape `Hβ.lower.pipe-completion-carries-the-stage-handle`
  // renders as an address. The call is the price of not writing that shape.
  //
  // 1,103 — and this is the first raise the medium can itemize BY CALLEE,
  // because the census now tallies what convicted each site
  // (`census_fact`). Its first reading reframes this whole line: 353 of the
  // 1,103 are calls to `int_to_str` — one leaf, a third of the count — so the
  // countdown is concentrated, not diffuse, and grounding that one row is
  // worth more than every raise above combined. This landing's own share is
  // the pattern render reading a constructor's declared field names through
  // `callee_params`: seventeen sites on the render family it reaches
  // (`render_pat_tokens`, `render_pat_shape`, `render_pat_fields`,
  // `render_pat_list`, `render_con_pattern`, `render_plist_inner`), each a
  // grounded leaf until it read the env. The other five are not itemized,
  // because the tally did not exist before this landing to compare against.
  //
  // None of these is the probe's 856, which counted chase EVENTS inside one
  // lower run. Four instruments, four denominators, one fact; recording all
  // of them is how the next reader avoids reconciling numbers that were
  // never the same.
  Bound({ceiling: 1103, shape: CsFreeRowCallee}),
  // 480 — the imperative loop in recursion's costume, counted across the
  // whole wheel and bounded for the first time 2026-09-21 (Morgan: "anytime
  // there is anything that could be written with the five topological
  // operators, do it"). The shape existed; nothing refused the next one.
  // The producer that dissolves the family is `iterate_range` (prelude): a
  // handle walk is `{ iterate_range(0, n) … result() } ~> collector`, and
  // eleven such walks in query.mn and graph.mn became folds the day this
  // bound was born (484 → 480 net, because the producer itself is one).
  // Every fold written against this number raises `CsFreeRowCallee` by one
  // — the two ratchets measure one defect, and it is
  // `Hβ.link.manifest-and-blob-emit-differently`'s: the flat judgment's end.
  //
  // 467 — three index walks in the formatter's pattern and config renders
  // became `map`/`join` stages when the pattern render learned named fields
  // (2026-09-23). The ceiling follows the count down.
  Bound({ceiling: 467, shape: CsIterationCostume}),
  // 136 — a gate told to look away, counted on the comments column. Each
  // marker is a bash pattern left imprecise (the control-keyword rule inside
  // a Reason string, the accumulator rule on a bounded stack push); the
  // count falls as each pattern is absorbed into a census shape that reads
  // structure instead of text (Phase 5.6's motion), and its zero is an
  // audit that needs no exemptions.
  Bound({ceiling: 136, shape: CsAuditSilenced}),
  // 732 — a product destructured by position with two or more slots
  // discarded (`FnStmt(n, _, _, _, _)`, `(_h, p, _s, _d)`), counted on
  // every match and let across the wheel the day Morgan's screenshot named
  // it (2026-09-21). The zero is every product carrying NAMED fields, so a
  // reader puns the field it wants by name; each constructor named retires
  // every one of its destructures at once, because `mentl fmt` renders a
  // positional pattern on a named constructor by name.
  //
  // 396 — named constructor fields, 2026-09-23. The census tallies the
  // product each site counts slots of (`census_fact`), and it named the
  // work: `N` 195, tuples 164, `TFun` 64, `FnStmt` 41, `Span` 28, `EfRow`
  // 21. Naming `N`, `TFun`, `FnStmt`, `Span`, `EfRow`, `EffectOpScheme`,
  // `TParam` and coverage's `SCon`, then an fmt sweep, took 738 to 391 with
  // no pattern written by hand. The tuples are the largest remainder, and
  // their form is a record, not a name on a position.
  Bound({ceiling: 391, shape: CsWildcardDestructure})
]

// The board: every bound answered by one live walk.
//
// The answer is `census_sites(shape)` — the walk's own result, not a number
// recovered from its rendering. That distinction is the landing: the old path
// ran this same walk, printed "N site(s)", and then asked a regex what N was,
// so a change to the SENTENCE could break the GATE. Nothing here can drift
// from the walk, because there is nothing between them.
fn board_read() with GraphRead + !Mutate + Alloc + Memory = board_bounds() |> map(bound_standing)

fn bound_standing(b) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Alloc + Memory = match b {
  Bound(r) => {
    let sites = census_sites(r.shape)
    (b, if len(sites) > r.ceiling { Over(sites) } else { Within(sites) })
  },
}

// One line, in the medium's voice: the shape, what it found, and — when the
// bound is breached — the fact that a count rose rather than a rule fired,
// which is the honest description of what a ratchet knows.
fn board_line(entry) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc + Intern = match entry {
  (b, standing) => match b {
    Bound(r) => match standing {
      Within(sites) => "  · {int_to_str(len(sites))} {census_label(r.shape)} — within {int_to_str(r.ceiling)}\n",
      Over(sites) => // A breach names WHERE, because the number alone is the one thing the
      // developer cannot act on. The sites come from the same walk that
      // decided the breach — one read, no second question.
      "  ✗ {int_to_str(len(sites))} {census_label(r.shape)} — ROSE past {int_to_str(r.ceiling)}\n{board_sites(sites)}",
    },
  },
}

fn board_sites(sites) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc + Intern =
  sites |> map(board_site_line) |> str_concat_all

fn board_site_line(h) with GraphRead + !Mutate + Memory + Alloc + Intern =
  "      {site_address(h)}\n"

fn board_breached(entry) with Pure = match entry {
  (_b, standing) => match standing {
    Within(_) => false,
    Over(_) => true,
  },
}
